        "title": "Nightmare · no safe rhythm",
        "kind": {
          "type": "Frame",
          "size": [
            640.0,
            138.0
          ],
          "text": "Nothing settles. A fast noise decides when bursts start and stop — irregular by design, quicker the faster you move. During a burst the pitch jumps to a new random place nine times a second (4–100 Hz) at 75–100 % intensity; between bursts it thumps at 4 Hz at 45 %. A hard pull-out fires a full one-second burst and lifts the floor (Limit Min 8 → 18). A sits at 8–32, B 6–30 and replays A 90 ms late with its own pitch. The Graph cap in Setup still wins."
        }
